{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"033aaa99019e7ddcc278635976cc4db3e7de01d0bfd3f316718f4cd3e709a222","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot receiver","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","src/rebar/review_bot/config.py","tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_redaction.py","infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","infra/gerrit/webhooks.config","infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","/webhook","/rerun","X-Rebar-Token","GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN","WEBHOOK_TOKEN","TokenRedactingFilter","install_access_log_redaction"],"problem_keywords":["credentials in logs","query string secret exposure","journald plaintext logging","authentication token leak"],"propositions":["Review-bot logs the webhook and rerun authentication token in plaintext via uvicorn's access log when the token is passed as a query parameter, exposing the credential to journald and any log consumers","The shared webhook token is the GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN (a Gerrit credential), making plaintext logging a critical security exposure that enables both Gerrit impersonation and unauthorized reviews","The fix moves token authentication from query string to X-Rebar-Token HTTP header and installs a TokenRedactingFilter to scrub any legacy query-param tokens from access logs while preserving route and status for observability","The previously-logged token must be rotated independently and tracked separately from the code fix, as the code change alone does not un-leak credentials already in journald or shared log excerpts"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787909584846741001,"uuid":"df52868d-801c-46b0-9c65-a20d2e4d2603"}